# Cursor global rules (hkarau)

Claude's copy lives in `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `~/.claude/rules/`. These
`.mdc` files are the Cursor dual-write. Claude `@` imports do not resolve
here, so each file is self-contained.

Do not copy any of this into a repo's `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`. In
apache/spark worktrees those files are tracked upstream.

| File | When |
|---|---|
| `style.mdc` | always -- voice, done-ness, where hacks belong |
| `defer-items.mdc` | always -- defer requests write `~/defered_items/projects/<date>_<desc>.md` |
| `always-run-tests.mdc` | always -- run tests, `/tmp/test-lock` (3 slots), Scala rebuild, `spark-presend` before push |
| `verify-and-review.mdc` | always -- claims, cross-review |
| `git-workflow.mdc` | always -- merge/rebuild/test/push, no amend after push |
| `spark-pyspark.mdc` | Spark worktrees -- venv, how to run tests |
| `spark-conventions.mdc` | Spark worktrees -- security JIRA exception, Closed vs Merged, PR scope |
| `spark-security-jira.mdc` | always -- no hole-describing tickets; innocuous titles maybe |

Helper scripts live in `~/mydotfiles/bin/` (the dotfiles repo; `~/bin` is a
symlink to it and is on `PATH`): `with-test-lock`,
`spark-compile-test-and-retry`, `spark-presend`, `rebase_update.sh`. They
find each other by resolving their own path, so repo moves never stale the
cross-references. No AI in them -- all result parsing is static (regex over
sbt/unittest output); if a parse gap shows up, fix the parser, do not shell
out to an agent.
Shared lock helper (same path Claude uses):

    bash ~/bin/with-test-lock -- <build-or-test-command>
    bash ~/bin/with-test-lock --status
